From b971c2bf247ae4912ff6bcb6dc15a9b67efbb5fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:47:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/49] Show pre-live face verification as a native QR code

startLive can ask for face verification with need_face_auth and a qr URL
(the fields the Windows client's FaceAuthPresenter reads). That now
becomes faceAuthQR: a native window shows the QR code for the Bilibili
app, polls IsUserIdentifiedByFaceAuth every two seconds and retries Go
live once verified, with a manual "verified, retry" fallback. Payloads
carrying only a risk voucher keep using Bilibili's verification page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
